    "home-founder-eyebrow": "A LETTER FROM THE FOUNDER",
    "home-founder-quote": "\"I was eighteen years old the first time I walked into a library.\"",
    "home-founder-p1": "I was born in Haiti. I crossed thirty-five countries building technology systems for companies most people have heard of. I watched France protect its cathedrals, Japan rebuild its shrines, Mexico fund museums for its pyramids.",
    "home-founder-p2": "Then I came home and looked at what Haiti's history had become. So I built three libraries in northern Haiti — Pilate, Ferrier, Ouanaminthe — serving more than 500,000 people. But libraries are only the beginning.",
    "home-founder-p3": "I am a father. I cannot stop thinking about Haiti. Levoila is what I am doing about it.",
