    "dispatches-1-cat": "HISTORY  ·  MAY 9",
    "dispatches-1-h3": "The Day the Citadelle Became a Place of Grief.",
    "dispatches-1-body": "On April 11, 2026, the largest fortress in the Western Hemisphere became the place where Haitian children died. This is what we owe them, and how we honor them now.",
    "dispatches-1-byline": "By the Editors  ·  4 min read",
    "dispatches-2-cat": "HISTORY  ·  MAY 5",
    "dispatches-2-h3": "What Henri Christophe Was Building.",
    "dispatches-2-body": "A king. A palace to rival Versailles. A statement, in stone, that a newly free Black nation could build whatever any European court could build. Two centuries later, we are answering him.",
    "dispatches-2-byline": "By the Editors  ·  7 min read",
    "dispatches-3-cat": "THE PEOPLE  ·  MAY 8",
    "dispatches-3-h3": "Meet the Master Mason of Milot.",
    "dispatches-3-body": "The hands that will rebuild the Citadelle have to know stone the way a violinist knows wood. We're profiling the woman who will lead that crew — and her apprentices from three nearby villages.",
    "dispatches-3-byline": "By the Editors  ·  5 min read",
    "dispatches-4-cat": "STEWARDS  ·  MAY 3",
    "dispatches-4-h3": "Phase One by the Numbers.",
    "dispatches-4-body": "Where the money is. Where it goes next. Which countries are joining fastest. Why 82% of every dollar leaves through a Haitian bank account.",
    "dispatches-4-byline": "By the Editors  ·  3 min read",
    "dispatches-5-cat": "THE TRUST  ·  APR 28",
    "dispatches-5-h3": "What \"Le Voilà\" Means in Five Languages.",
    "dispatches-5-body": "Why our name is the phrase a parent says when they show a child something for the first time. And what each of our five operating languages adds to it.",
    "dispatches-5-byline": "By the Editors  ·  4 min read",
    "dispatches-6-cat": "FOUNDER  ·  APR 22",
    "dispatches-6-h3": "The Three Libraries That Started All This.",
    "dispatches-6-body": "Before Levoila, there was the Universal Learning Centre. Before that, a boy in Ferrier who had never seen a library until he was eighteen. The full story of how 500,000 readers came to be.",
    "dispatches-6-byline": "By Jacques Medina Jean  ·  8 min read",
    "dispatches-7-cat": "THE TRUST  ·  APR 18",
    "dispatches-7-h3": "The Sovereignty Compact, in 800 Words.",
    "dispatches-7-body": "How a 501(c)(3) charity in Texas writes a long-term lease with a sovereign nation, without owning anything, and pays the nation a royalty for the privilege. The whole legal architecture, explained plainly.",
    "dispatches-7-byline": "By the Editors  ·  6 min read",
    "dispatches-8-cat": "STEWARDS  ·  APR 14",
    "dispatches-8-h3": "Behind the Wall of Founders.",
    "dispatches-8-body": "The first 10,000 Stewards will be engraved into the entrance of the Citadelle. Here is how the engraving works, what stone we'll use, and the local craftsperson who will cut your name with her hands.",
    "dispatches-8-byline": "By the Editors  ·  5 min read",
    "dispatches-9-cat": "THE SITES  ·  APR 9",
    "dispatches-9-h3": "Why We Look to Gabon.",
    "dispatches-9-body": "Lopé-Okanda holds rock engravings tens of thousands of years old — among the longest continuous records of human presence on Earth. Here's the case for Gabon as Levoila's second country.",
    "dispatches-9-byline": "By the Editors  ·  7 min read",
    "dispatches-10-cat": "THE SITES  ·  APR 3",
    "dispatches-10-h3": "Fort Liberté, in Three Walls.",
    "dispatches-10-body": "A French naval stronghold. A redoubt of the war of independence. A bay fortress quietly returning to the sea. What we know about Fort Liberté, and what its three walls remember.",
    "dispatches-10-byline": "By the Editors  ·  6 min read",
    "dispatches-11-cat": "THE TRUST  ·  MAR 29",
    "dispatches-11-h3": "Six Sites Enter the Quarterly Vote.",
    "dispatches-11-body": "São Jorge da Mina in Ghana. Bet Maryam in Lalibela. The Old Cairo Aqueduct. Tlatelolco. Bagamoyo. Petra. Six places. Six communities. The Stewards decide which two enter Sovereignty Compact next.",
    "dispatches-11-byline": "By the Editors  ·  5 min read",
    "dispatches-12-cat": "THE PEOPLE  ·  MAR 22",
    "dispatches-12-h3": "The Word in Kreyòl.",
    "dispatches-12-body": "\"Si yo bliye, nou pa bliye.\" If they forget, we do not. A Haitian saying that became the first sentence Levoila ever wrote in Kreyòl. The story of how the brand voice in each of our five languages was forged.",
    "dispatches-12-byline": "By the Editors  ·  4 min read",
    "dispatches-loadmore": "Load more dispatches",
